I commented on #1158 and closed it, and left the other eight issues alone.

#1158 (closed): commit 24770172 fixed it. A new test runs the built yoyo against a stub server and records what is actually sent for --provider google:
• Without `--max-tokens`: the request has no generationConfig at all, so the guessed 8192 never goes out.
• With `--max-tokens 1000`: it sends maxOutputTokens == 1000. This shows the stub really reads that field, so the first result is a real absence.

The warning for Google no longer says "every reply is capped at 8192". It now says yoyo sends no output cap, Google uses the model's own default, and you can set max_tokens to cap replies. The docs in docs/src/configuration/models.md were corrected to match.

No comment on the rest (#1122, #991, #1147, #1134, #1121, #1102, #1100, #1094, #1064, #1012): this session's commits didn't touch them, and I had nothing new to add. On #1122 and #991 I posted the last reply and didn't promise a follow-up. Task 1 (user deny rules now catch quoted or escaped spellings of a command) doesn't belong to any open issue in this list, so it got no comment.
